      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a9836fe8-3929-548b-8519-a349183182d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Philip Quast, Colm Wilkinson, Michael Ball, Lea Salonga, Judy Kuhn, Ruthie Henshall, Michael Maguire, Alun Armstrong, Jenny Galloway, Adam Searles, Hannah Chick, John Caird, David Charles Abell, Sandra Sciberras, Victoria Thaine, Susie Porter\n- Productions: Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert, The Caterpillar Wish\n- Organizations: Royal Philharmonic Orchestra\n- Topics: casting, musical theatre, film\n\nFacts:\n- Philip Quast was born on 30 July 1957 and is an Australian actor and singer.\n- Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert featured its 10th Anniversary cast with Colm Wilkinson as Jean Valjean, Philip Quast as Inspector Javert, Michael Ball as Marius Pontmercy, Lea Salonga as Éponine, Judy Kuhn as Cosette, Ruthie Henshall as Fantine, Michael Maguire as Enjolras, Alun Armstrong as Thénardier, Jenny Galloway as Madame Thénardier, Adam Searles as Gavroche, and Hannah Chick as Young Cosette.\n- Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert was directed by John Caird.\n- The performers in Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert were chosen from the London, Broadway, and Australian productions of the show.\n- The Royal Philharmonic Orchestra performed for Les Misérables: The Dream Cast in Concert and was conducted by David Charles Abell.\n- Philip Quast has won the Laurence Olivier Award for Best Actor in a Musical three times, which is the most of any actor to date.\n- The Caterpillar Wish, also known as Caterpillar Wish, is a 2006 Australian coming-of-age film directed by Sandra Sciberras.\n- The Caterpillar Wish stars an ensemble cast including Victoria Thaine, Susie Porter, and Philip Quast.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
